/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A filter is a frequency-dependent voltage divider.
   - The cutoff is the frequency where gain falls to 1/√2 = 0.707 of the pass-band value.
   - Hlow is voltage gain; f is signal frequency in Hz; fc is cutoff frequency in Hz.
   - Hhigh is voltage gain of a first-order high-pass; f and fc are in Hz.
   - The simplest low-pass is a resistor R in series and capacitor C to ground.
   - R is series resistance in ohms; C is capacitance in farads; fc is in Hz.
   - An active filter uses an op-amp to give gain and a low output impedance.
   - A pre-amplifier is the first amplifier after the sensor.
   - A differential amplifier has two inputs, V1 and V2, and responds to their difference Vd = V1 − V2.
   - Ad is differential gain in V/V; Acm is common-mode gain in V/V; CMRR is in dB.
*/
